---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our story"
  description="Why Red Mountain Soap builds a small, place-based soap line in Ivins, Utah."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
      <h1>Made where the desert meets the mountain.</h1>
      <p>
        Red Mountain Soap is a small production-minded soap business in Ivins, Utah—close enough to the cliffs that “red mountain” is a description before it is a brand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="shell story-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why six products</p>
        <h2>A line people can understand at a glance.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The opening collection is intentionally compact. Each bar needs a clear role, a distinct scent story, and a reason to remain in production.
        </p>
        <p>
          That discipline matters behind the scenes, too. Small batches require planning around ingredients, molds, cure time, sellable inventory, and honest costs. The website should make the result feel simple because the operational work is not.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="story-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Brand compass</p>
        <h2>Rugged, refined, and restrained.</h2>
        <p>
          The visual language borrows from National Park posters, trail markers, old field guides, matte paper, and carved emblems—without turning Southern Utah into a costume.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What stays visible</p>
          <h2>The useful details.</h2>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="content-grid">
        <article class="content-card">
          <div class="content-card__icon">01</div>
          <h3>Place</h3>
          <p>Ivins and the broader Southern Utah landscape shape the names, palette, photography, and scent stories.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="content-card">
          <div class="content-card__icon">02</div>
          <h3>Process</h3>
          <p>Cold-process batches are tracked through production and cure before they become available to sell.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="content-card">
          <div class="content-card__icon">03</div>
          <h3>Clarity</h3>
          <p>Ingredient panels, weights, scent descriptions, and policies should answer questions without a cloud of adjectives.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
